  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or take a screenshot, so none of the visuals or light levels have been seen. Spot intensity (60), env intensity and bloom were chosen from the docs' defaults and may need adjusting after a first look.\n\n- **Pedestal:** four stepped marble boxes. Their texture is a 1024² Carrara pattern generated in code. It uses periodic fractal noise to warp two sets of sine stripes, plus ridged-noise veins and soft grey halos. The material is polished: roughness 0.16, clearcoat 0.6. Each step uses a different UV scale and offset.\n- **Trophy:** a custom-geometry lathe builds the foot, stem, knop, cup, rolled rim and inside surface in polished gold (metallic 1, roughness 0.14, strong env reflection). Two handles are tubes swept along curves. A darker, rougher gold band sits on the cup with two bright gold fillets, and there is a small ring on the stem.\n- **Base:** two stacked blocks of black polished stone. A thin gold plate with three dark-gold engraved lines sits on the front.\n- **Room:** a dark warm gallery with a floor, three walls and two glowing windows with frames. The environment comes from `environments.neutral` (a code-generated room probe with lamps), tinted warm. I used it because the HDRI path only accepts URL-based asset references. The windows are real scene geometry, so the gold does not reflect them.\n- **Lighting:** a warm shadow-casting spotlight from above and in front, a faint cool fill, a subtle cool rim light and light bloom.\n- **Camera:** it oscillates ±15° around the trophy over a 24 s period, set each frame with `app.camera.setPose`. If `app.camera` were undefined, the camera would simply stay fixed.\n- **Globals:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is `{ materials: ['marble','gold','darkstone'], cameraAzimuthDeg }`, updated every frame. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first frame callback.\n\n",
